        "id": 253140,
        "name": "Trajector",
        "username": "Trajector",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
        "created_at": "2023-07-10T19:01:53.083Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"dprcooke\" data-post=\"5\" data-topic=\"30104\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/dprcooke/48/1961_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> dprcooke:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>But have they ever talked about why there isn’t a mainline hero who’s archetype is similar to Spiderman?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Not necessarily in terms of the stories, but in terms of gameplay, I’ve been looking to Void Guard Writhe for this. I think he has the right sense of agility, of balancing vulnerability vs “swinging away,” and of causing special effects to tie up or confuse enemy targets.</p>",
